[ext_resource type="Script" path="res://src/Economy/ShopInvestmentTier.cs" id="3_tier"]

; Gilda Ironmonger (Phase 38L) - metal traded rather than metal worked, which is the whole distinction
; between her and Bryn one street north. He forges; she buys and sells what forges eat and produce.
;
; The iron dagger exists so her `weapon` specialty is a shelf. Before 38L the tag had exactly one member
; and a "weapons specialist" specialised in one sword - the premium was authored, validated, and applied
; to a single row.
;
; One investment rung, not Bryn's two: a stall is a smaller thing to buy into than a forge, and the ladder
; should read as proportional to what is being bought. It opens the steel sword, which she otherwise keeps
; back for people she knows.
;
; 38S: she haggles at 40 for -2, harder and dearer than Aldreth's 50 for -1 across the square. A market
; trader who has heard every line before is the reason in fiction; in play it is the second rung of the
; same lesson, and the two counters being a minute apart is what makes the difference legible at all.

